# BLAST peer hints, one per line, in addnode= format
# (host[:port]; port defaults to 64640 if omitted).
#
# This file is consulted by init.sh; non-empty entries are rendered into
# data/blast.conf as addnode= directives. Blank lines and lines starting
# with # are ignored.
#
# 2026-05-16: empty. All three DNS seeds in src/chainparams.cpp
#
#     seed.blastblastblast.com
#     seed1.blastblastblast.com
#     seed2.blastblastblast.com
#
# plus their bare-domain / www / testseed siblings all wildcard-resolve to
# the same single GCP IP 35.220.144.141 (PTR
# 141.144.220.35.bc.googleusercontent.com.). TCP 64640 on that IP is
# closed; the host responds only on TCP 80. This is a wildcard A-record on
# a single dormant GCP instance, not a populated DNS seeder — the strongest
# single signal that the BLAST network is dead.
#
# Add an addnode= here only when a working peer surfaces (BitcoinTalk
# 2547036 outreach, a former pool operator, an archived peers.dat, etc.).
